Root cause:
The bug was caused by the use of indirect calls in the MSR (Model-Specific Register) operations related to SPEC_CTRL during the IBRS (Indirect Branch Restricted Speculation) restore path. This approach was problematic because it could potentially allow speculative execution of incorrect indirect branch targets, which undermines the security measures intended to prevent such speculative execution vulnerabilities. The patch replaces these indirect calls with direct calls to `native_wrmsrl()` and `native_read_msr()`, improving both security and performance.
